  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    # Find the 3-filled rectangle\n    rows, cols = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    threes = [(r,c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols) if grid[r][c] == 3]\n    min_r = min(r for r,c in threes)\n    max_r = max(r for r,c in threes)\n    min_c = min(c for r,c in threes)\n    max_c = max(c for r,c in threes)\n    \n    h = max_r - min_r + 1\n    w = max_c - min_c + 1\n    \n    # Find the symmetric counterpart to recover original values\n    # The grid has symmetry. Find what should be under the 3s by looking at symmetric positions.\n    # Check which quadrant the 3-block is in and use opposite quadrant\n    \n    result = []\n    for r in range(min_r, max_r + 1):\n        row = []\n        for c in range(min_c, max_c + 1):\n            # Try mirror across center\n            mr = rows - 1 - r\n            mc = cols - 1 - c\n            row.append(grid[mr][mc])\n        result.append(row)\n    return result",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    # Find the 3-filled rectangle\n    rows, cols = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    threes = [(r,c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols) if grid[r][c] == 3]\n    min_r = min(r for r,c in threes)\n    max_r = max(r for r,c in threes)\n    min_c = min(c for r,c in threes)\n    max_c = max(c for r,c in threes)\n    \n    h = max_r - min_r + 1\n    w = max_c - min_c + 1\n    \n    # Find the symmetric counterpart to recover original values\n    # The grid has symmetry. Find what should be under the 3s by looking at symmetric positions.\n    # Check which quadrant the 3-block is in and use opposite quadrant\n    \n    result = []\n    for r in range(min_r, max_r + 1):\n        row = []\n        for c in range(min_c, max_c + 1):\n            # Try mirror across center\n            mr = rows - 1 - r\n            mc = cols - 1 - c\n            row.append(grid[mr][mc])\n        result.append(row)\n    return result",
